Revision history for Langertha-Holmgang

{{$NEXT}}
  - Initial release
  - Deterministic tool-use benchmarks for language models: a case gives the
    model a task and tools in a simulated world, and the rules grade the
    end state of that world, never the wording of the answer
  - Suite format 2 (suite.yaml plus cases/*.yaml) loads into objects that
    keep the values as written; every case is linted on load, including two
    mock runs, and a case that fails lint does not load
  - Worlds with tool dispatch, observations, handlers and Kolon output, and
    simulators for the device types linux (bash grammar and many services),
    routeros and ios, plus the answer world kueche; a simulator plugin
    contract (Role::Simulator, Role::AnswerWorld, registry); a simulator
    that fails in Perl never shows its error to the model, the call answers
    a generic tool error and the gap is recorded
  - Grader with rules on the end state and on the calls, and seven statuses:
    passed, failed, uncertain (a simulation gap was hit), turn_limit, and
    the not-measured error, context_exceeded and no_vision
  - Runner over any Langertha engine through Target, with turn limit and
    tokens, finish reason and calls per turn; Langertha::Engine::Virtual
    mock models run a case without a network; Haystack generates long,
    deterministic inputs
  - Target classifies a failed turn as context_exceeded, no_vision or error
    and scrubs its error text: the engine's key, credentials in URLs,
    Authorization and Bearer values, provider key shapes, die locations and
    host paths never reach a result
  - Report: the JSON report (holmgang_report 1), written, read and merged
    without double counting
  - Evaluation: rates per topic with case weights, overall as the mean of
    topics, curves per length tier, verdicts against a threshold with pass^k
    and hard cases, and the comparison of targets as text, Markdown or JSON
  - bin/holmgang with the commands lint, run and report. lint loads exactly
    as a run does; run takes any Langertha engine by name (--model, --url,
    --option) or the network-free mock-solution and mock-text, with
    --variant, --repeat and --report, and no key on the command line;
    report evaluates report files with thresholds from --suite. Exit 0 ok,
    1 refused, verdict not ok or no case answered by the target, 2 usage or
    setup error. Errors on stderr carry no Perl location
  - Three invented example suites under share/suites: demo-linux,
    demo-lamp and demo-haystack, found with
    File::ShareDir::dist_dir('Langertha-Holmgang').'/suites'
  - Documentation: an overview in Langertha::Holmgang, the suite format 2
    reference in ::Loader, rules and statuses in ::Grader, the simulator
    contract in ::Role::Simulator, and a README with a quick start
  - Not yet: cases and suites written in a Perl DSL; Langertha::Holmgang
    exports nothing so far
